<item>
  <title>Estimating the distribution of a scan statistic by simulation</title>
  <dc:creator>Alexandru Amărioarei</dc:creator>
  <link>https://alexamarioarei.github.io/blog/posts/2026-11-20-exemplu/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<p>This is the first post on this blog, and it starts with the question behind scan statistics: when a sequence of observations shows a cluster of events, how surprising is that cluster under pure chance?</p>
<section id="the-problem" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
<p>Let <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?X_1,%20X_2,%20%5Cdots,%20X_N"> be independent Bernoulli random variables with parameter <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?p">. For a window of length <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?m">, the one-dimensional discrete scan statistic is</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AS_m(N)%20=%20%5Cmax_%7B1%20%5Cle%20i%20%5Cle%20N-m+1%7D%20%5C;%20%5Csum_%7Bk=i%7D%5E%7Bi+m-1%7D%20X_k%20.%0A"></p>
<p>We are interested in <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cmathbb%7BP%7D%5Cbig(S_m(N)%20%5Cge%20k%5Cbig)">, the probability that somewhere in the sequence a window of length <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?m"> contains at least <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k"> successes.</p>
<div id="def-scan" class="theorem definition">
<p><span class="theorem-title"><strong>Definition 1 (Scan statistic)</strong></span> For a sequence <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?(X_k)"> and a length <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?m">, the <em>scan statistic</em> is the largest number of successes contained in a window of <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?m"> consecutive observations.</p>
</div>
<p>Simulation is the most direct way to estimate this probability, and a useful check for exact formulas and approximations.</p>
</section>
<section id="monte-carlo-estimation-in-r" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="monte-carlo-estimation-in-r">Monte Carlo estimation in R</h2>
<p>The simplest estimator is the relative frequency over <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?n"> independent simulations:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cwidehat%7BP%7D_n%20=%20%5Cfrac%7B1%7D%7Bn%7D%20%5Csum_%7Br=1%7D%5E%7Bn%7D%20%5Cmathbf%7B1%7D%5C%7BS%5E%7B(r)%7D_m(N)%20%5Cge%20k%5C%7D,%0A%5Cqquad%0A%5Coperatorname%7Bse%7D%5Cbig(%5Cwidehat%7BP%7D_n%5Cbig)%20%5Capprox%20%5Csqrt%7B%5Cfrac%7B%5Cwidehat%7BP%7D_n%20(1-%5Cwidehat%7BP%7D_n)%7D%7Bn%7D%7D%20.%0A"></p>
<p>The window sums are obtained from cumulative sums, so each simulated sequence is scanned in linear time.</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb1-1">scan_1d <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">function</span>(x, m) {</span>
<span id="cb1-2">  <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># window sums of length m, computed from cumulative sums</span></span>
<span id="cb1-3">  s <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">cumsum</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0</span>, x))</span>
<span id="cb1-4">  <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">max</span>(s[(m <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>)<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">length</span>(s)] <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span> s[<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span><span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">:</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">length</span>(s) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span> m)])</span>
<span id="cb1-5">}</span>
<span id="cb1-6"></span>
<span id="cb1-7"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">set.seed</span>(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">2026</span>)</span>
<span id="cb1-8">N <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1000</span>; m <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">20</span>; p <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.05</span>; k <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">6</span></span>
<span id="cb1-9">S <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">replicate</span>(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">10000</span>, <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">scan_1d</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">rbinom</span>(N, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>, p), m))</span>
<span id="cb1-10"></span>
<span id="cb1-11">p_hat <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">mean</span>(S <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&gt;=</span> k)</span>
<span id="cb1-12">se    <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sqrt</span>(p_hat <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">*</span> (<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span> <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span> p_hat) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">length</span>(S))</span>
<span id="cb1-13"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">round</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">estimate =</span> p_hat, <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">std_error =</span> se), <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">4</span>)</span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code> estimate std_error 
   0.0709    0.0026 </code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>For <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?N%20=%201000">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?m%20=%2020"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?p%20=%200.05">, the probability that some window contains at least <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%206"> successes is estimated at 0.0709, with a standard error of 0.0026. Within a single window the expected number of successes is only <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?mp%20=%201">, so it is the scanning over <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?N%20-%20m%20+%201"> overlapping windows that makes such a cluster likely.</p>
<p>Figure&nbsp;1 shows the whole simulated distribution of <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?S_%7B20%7D(1000)">; the values at or above <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%206"> are highlighted.</p>
